{{<shell}}{{$content}}
<h1>Settings</h1>
<p class="hint">What this community is, as opposed to how the machine it runs on is set up. Everything
  here is kept in this community's own database and can be changed from this page.</p>
<p class="hint">Sign-in policy, credentials, what a program connecting here may do, and the limits on
  what a request may carry are deliberately <strong>not</strong> here. Those live in
  {{#configFile}}<code>{{configFile}}</code>{{/configFile}}{{^configFile}}the config file{{/configFile}},
  where they are changed by somebody with access to the machine and reviewed by reading a file &mdash;
  a browser session that has been taken over must not be able to move any of them.</p>

{{^setupDone}}
<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>Nobody has been through the setup here yet.</strong> This community is running on
    defaults that were guessed rather than chosen. The walkthrough is four screens and asks only
    about the ones where being wrong is visible to everybody.</p>
  <p><a class="button" href="{{setupUrl}}">Go through the setup</a></p>
</div>
{{/setupDone}}

<form method="post" action="{{action}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{csrf}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="action" value="save">
  {{#groups}}
  <h2>{{group}}</h2>
  {{#settings}}
  <div class="field">
    <label for="{{field}}"><strong>{{label}}</strong></label>
    {{#isText}}<input type="text" id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}" value="{{value}}">{{/isText}}
    {{#isNumber}}<input type="number" id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}" value="{{value}}">{{/isNumber}}
    {{#isMultiline}}<textarea id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}" rows="4">{{value}}</textarea>{{/isMultiline}}
    {{#isChoice}}
    <select id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}">
      {{#options}}<option value="{{value}}"{{#selected}} selected{{/selected}}>{{value}}</option>{{/options}}
    </select>
    {{/isChoice}}
    {{#isBool}}
    <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="{{field}}" name="{{field}}"{{#checked}} checked{{/checked}}> on</label>
    {{/isBool}}
    <p class="hint">{{help}}</p>
    <p class="dim"><code>{{key}}</code>
      {{#overridden}}<span class="pill blue">set here</span>{{/overridden}}
      {{^overridden}}<span class="pill">from the config file, or the built-in default</span>{{/overridden}}
    </p>
  </div>
  {{/settings}}
  {{/groups}}
  <div class="rowactions">
    <button type="submit">Save settings</button>
  </div>
</form>

<h2>Putting one back</h2>
<p class="hint">Clearing a box and saving removes this community's answer, so whatever the config
  file says &mdash; or the built-in default &mdash; comes back. Nothing is stored as an empty value,
  because a community that emptied a box could then never get the default again.</p>
{{/content}}{{/shell}}
